  "bio": {
    "eyebrow": "About Dr Gerami",
    "heading_lead": "Meet",
    "heading_warm": "Dr Gerami.",
    "paragraphs": [
      "Dr Sam Gerami is an independent Consultant Specialist GP (ABN: 73 693 511 256) (MED0002572916) consulting at the Earlwood centre.",
      "Dr Sam graduated from Australian National University Medical School and has worked as a doctor at Gosford and Wyong Hospitals, Royal Prince Alfred Hospital, and Dubbo Hospital, working across a range of specialities including Paediatrics, O&G, Surgery, and Internal Medicine. He continues to work at Royal Prince Alfred Hospital occasionally, and also holds an associate lecturer position at University of Sydney Medical School doing research and teaching for medical students.",
      "Dr Sam is interested in all aspects of general practice and particularly enjoys looking after entire families. He prides himself on a non-judgemental, empathetic approach to every consultation. Outside of the clinic he likes to spend time with his family, go for a bike ride, or read.",
      "Dr Sam speaks Farsi in addition to English."
    ]
  },
